Bilaspuri (Kahluri; ISO 639-3 kfs; Glottocode bila1253) is a Western Pahari language of Bilaspur district, Himachal Pradesh, with about 300,000 speakers (2011), counted in the census under Punjabi. Very little dedicated material was found.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
No primers, textbooks or school programmes for Bilaspuri were found in search results.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Wikipedia, Bilaspuri: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bilaspuri}
\item Wikipedia, Kahluri: \url{https://Www.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kahluri}
\item Omniglot page on Bilaspuri (scripts, Takri and Devanagari): \url{https://omniglot.com/writing/bilaspuri.htm}
\item Linguistic Survey of India, Himachal Pradesh volume (PARI library; includes a chapter on Bilaspuri/Kahluri; contents not verified in detail): \url{https://ruralindiaonline.org/ml/library/resource/linguistic-survey-of-india---himachal-pradesh/}
\end{itemize}

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
None found.

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
None found. No dedicated dictionary was located.

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
The language is written today mainly in Devanagari, historically in a Takri variant. Without published teaching materials, a curriculum would depend on new fieldwork and community input.
